"Flip-sort and combinatorial aspects of pop-stack sorting (https://arxiv.org/abs/2003.04912)\nciteturn9academia12 [wordlim: 200] Published: 6.7 years ago; Title: Flip-sort and combinatorial aspects of pop-stack sorting\nTitle: Flip-sort and combinatorial aspects of pop-stack sorting\nAuthors: Andrei Asinowski, Cyril Banderier, Benjamin Hackl\nDate: Tue Mar 10 18:06:59 2020\n\nFlip-sort is a natural sorting procedure which raises fascinating combinatorial questions. It finds its roots in the seminal work of Knuth on stack-based sorting algorithms and leads to many links with permutation patterns. We present several structural, enumerative, and algorithmic results on permutations that need few (resp. many) iterations of this procedure to be sorted. In particular, we give the shape of the permutations after one iteration, and characterize several families of permutations related to the best and worst cases of flip-sort. En passant, we also give some links between pop-stack sorting, automata, and lattice paths, and introduce several tactics of bijective proofs which have their own interest.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nFlip-sort and combinatorial aspects of pop-stack sorting | Discrete Mathematics & Theoretical Computer Science | Discrete Mathematics & Theoretical Computer Science (https://dmtcs.episciences.org/en/articles/6196)\nciteturn9search0 [wordlim: 200] Published: 5.5 years ago; Crawled: last month; # Flip-sort and combinatorial aspects of pop-stack sorting ... Download article Open on arXiv ... # Flip-sort and combinatorial aspects of pop-stack sorting\n\nArticle\n\n# Flip-sort and combinatorial aspects of pop-stack sorting\n\nAndrei Asinowski , Cyril Banderier, Benjamin Hackl\n\nDownload articleOpen on arXiv\n\nPublication details\n\nSubmitted on\n\nMarch 12, 2020\n\nAccepted on\n\nApril 7, 2021\n\nPublished on\n\nApril 30, 2021\n\nLast modified on\n\nMarch 31, 2025\n\nSpecial issue 22\n\nvol. 22:2, Permutation Patterns 2019\n\nSpecial issues\n\nDOI\n\n10.46298/dmtcs.6196\n\nLicense\n\narXiv.org - Non-exclusive license to distribute\n\n# Flip-sort and combinatorial aspects of pop-stack sorting\n\nAndrei Asinowski , Cyril Banderier, Benjamin Hackl\n\nAbstract\n\nFlip-sort is a natural sorting procedure which raises fascinating combinatorial questions. It finds its roots in the seminal work of Knuth on stack-based sorting algorithms and leads to many links with permutation patterns. We present several structural, enumerative, and algorithmic results on permutations that need few (resp. many) iterations of this procedure to be sorted. In particular, we give the shape of the permutations after one iteration, and characterize several families of permutations related to the best and worst cases of flip-sort. En passant, we also give some links between pop-stack sorting, automata, and lattice paths, and introduce several tactics of bijective proofs which have their own interest. Comment: This v3 just updates the journal reference, according to the publisher wish\n\nKeywords\n\n  * Mathematics - Combinatorics\n  * Computer Science - Discrete Mathematics\n  * Computer Science - Data Structures and Algorithms\n  * Computer Science - Formal Languages and Automata Theory\n  * 05A05, 05A19, 05A15, 05A16--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nFlip-sort and combinatorial aspects of pop-stack sorting - MaRDI portal (https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/wiki/Flip-sort_and_combinatorial_aspects_of_pop-stack_sorting)\nciteturn9search1 [wordlim: 200] Published: 4.5 years ago; Crawled: 2 months ago; # Flip-sort and combinatorial aspects of pop-stack sorting ... Full work available at URL https://arxiv.org/abs/2003.04912, https://dmtcs.episciences.org/7411 ... This page was built for publication: Flip-sort and combinatorial aspects of pop-stack sorting\n# Flip-sort and combinatorial aspects of pop-stack sorting\n\nFrom MaRDI portal\n\n\nMaRDI QIDQ50